<!-- About Section -->
<section class="about">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-header">
            <h2 class="section-title">About Me</h2>
        </div>
    
        <div class="about-content">
            <div class="about-text">
                <p>

I am a dedicated researcher and Postdoctoral Associate at Purdue University. I hold a Ph.D. in Civil Engineering (Water Resource Engineering) and an M.S. in Environmental Engineering from Florida International University (FIU), in addition to an M.S. in Mechanical Engineering (Fluid Mechanics and CFD). My research is centered on solving complex challenges in water resources, environmental science, and biomedical engineering through advanced computational modeling and artificial intelligence. 
</p><p>
My experience spans computational fluid dynamics (CFD), machine learning, and hardware prototyping. In water resource engineering, I specialize in developing and validating 3D numerical models for storm sewer geyser eruptions using OpenFOAM and deploying AI and digital twin models for managing stormwater infrastructure. My work in biomedical engineering includes modeling magnetic drug targeting in blood vessels and analyzing biomagnetic fluid flow using CFD. I also apply deep learning algorithms (CNNs) for diverse applications, such as the segmentation of brain lesions in MRI images , real-time prediction of air-water volume fractions , and diagnosing fatigue foot from biomechanical data. Furthermore, I have designed and prototyped an autonomous robot for surface water trash collection.
</p><p>
In addition to my research, I am actively involved in the academic community. I previously served as Laboratory Manager I at FIU, where I directed research and teaching laboratories, managed detailed equipment and chemical inventories, and developed comprehensive laboratory safety protocols compliant with OSHA and EPA standards. Academically, I am a Guest Editor for a special issue of Pharmaceutics (Present) and have served as a Guest Editor for the Journal of Healthcare Engineering.

                </p>
                
                <div class="research-interests">
                    <h3>Research Interests</h3>
                    <div class="interests-grid">
                        <div class="interest-item">
                            <i class="fas fa-water"></i>
                            <span>Water Resource Engineering</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="interest-item">
                            <i class="fas fa-microscope"></i>
                            <span>Environmental Science</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="interest-item">
                            <i class="fas fa-heart-pulse"></i>
                            <span>Biomedical Engineering</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="interest-item">
                            <i class="fas fa-wind"></i>
                            <span>Computational Fluid Dynamics</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="interest-item">
                            <i class="fas fa-chart-line"></i>
                            <span>Signal Processing</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="interest-item">
                            <i class="fas fa-robot"></i>
                            <span>Machine Learning</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>


